  'SessionId' => 'e05eaa71b2aa67845b0742890b1a5987',
  'forumId' => '57',
  'title' => 'Sorrento wedding HELP!! ',
  'postContent' => 'Sorrento wedding: where to begin and what sort of budget?

Posted: Yesterday at 17:17
Hello fellow brides 2 be


I\'m starting with the original line \'this is my first post\'  but it is...in fact this is my first post in any forum. I\'m normally the one this sits reading forums, searching for an answer that Google has directed me to! In fact I tried that several times over the last few weeks but can\'t find a direct answer.


My fiancé and I are planning on marrying in Sorrento in 2017 either June or July. I\'m struggling to do much planning because I can\'t book anything until a later date...or can I? (that\'s not a rhetorical questions btw). I had originally thought I had to book everything through a travel agent, then I\'ve read about wedding planners...I\'ve looked up a few and found a couple of planners I like. Do I use both?


In all honesty the more homework I\'ve done on the matter the more of a pickle iv\'e got myself in.


Basically I want to know, where do I start when planning a wedding in Sorrento?


Secondly, could anyone provide me with details of rough costs? We are thinking about a budget of around £15k for the entire wedding. I\'m not sure that\'s do-able because I can only see the odd prices online but they\'re from a few years ago so I\'m only going by guestimates. Is there any super organised bride that could provide me with almost up to date itemised costs? I hope this doesn\'t sound like a cheeky request, I\'m just trying to get organised and make a realistic budget!


P.s we have chosen our wedding venue, the cloisters of San Francisco :) 

',
  'follow' => 'False',
  'sessionId' => 'e05eaa71b2aa67845b0742890b1a5987',
)
